  "title": "Scary Monsters",
  "country": "UK",
  "released": "1980-09-12",
  "notes": "Full title (as it appears on cover): Scary Monsters ... ... And Super Creeps\n\nIssued in a matte finish card picture sleeve with a folded 'poster' lyrics insert printed in sepia brown. Printing on one side only; back side is empty.\n\nBlack RCA paper labels with silver print indicating 'Stereo'.\n\n[Lyrics insert]\n[Tracks A1 to B2, B4 & B5] Copyright ©1980 by Bewlay Bros. Music + Fleur Music Ltd.\n[Track B3] Copyright ©1979 by Warner Bros. Music Ltd.\n\n[Labels]\n℗ 1980 RCA Corporation\nManufactured by RCA Ltd. England. From Master Recordings of RCA Corp.\n[Label Side A]\nAll tracks published by Bewlay Bros. Music/Fleur Music\n[Label Side B]\n[Track B3] Warner Bros. Music Ltd.\nTracks 1,2,4,5 published by Bewlay Bros. Music/Fleur Music\n\n[Spine ('s' for stereo in black circle)] \nRCA Ⓢ BOW LP 2   Cassette BOW K 2\n\n[Rear sleeve]\nSleeve © 1980 RCA Records.\n\nRecorded: Power Station, New York.\n\nRoy Bittan appears courtesy of the [url=https://www.discogs.com/artist/408247]E Street Band[/url]\nRobert Fripp appears courtesy of [l64547]\nPete Townshend appears courtesy of [l38030]\n\nA small number of copies were pressed on [url=http://www.discogs.com/David-Bowie-Scary-Monsters/release/2490014]purple vinyl[/url].\n\nCover artwork based on the photographs of [a1363971] commonly known as Duffy.\n\nRunouts are etched.\nVariant 37 and 43, side B, TOWNHOUSE is stamped.",
  "released_formatted": "12 Sep 1980",
